          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "illia.polosukhin@gmail.com",
          "x": 238.02,
          "y": 343.64,
          "width": 135.95,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f4",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "Abstract",
          "x": 283.76,
          "y": 382.83,
          "width": 44.49,
          "size": 11.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f2",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "The dominant sequence transduction models are based on complex recurrent or",
          "x": 143.56,
          "y": 411,
          "width": 324.74,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "convolutional neural networks that include an encoder and a decoder. The best",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 421.91,
          "width": 324.26,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "performing models also connect the encoder and decoder through an attention",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 432.82,
          "width": 324.26,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "mechanism. We propose a new simple network architecture, the Transformer,",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 443.73,
          "width": 325.51,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "based solely on attention mechanisms, dispensing with recurrence and convolutions",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 454.64,
          "width": 324.27,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "entirely.",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 465.55,
          "width": 32.93,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "x": 176.8,
          "y": 465.55,
          "width": 6.01,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "Experiments on two machine translation tasks show these models to",
          "x": 182.93,
          "y": 465.55,
          "width": 285.2,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "be superior in quality while being more parallelizable and requiring significantly",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 476.46,
          "width": 324.62,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "less time to train. Our model achieves 28.4 BLEU on the WMT 2014 English-",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 487.37,
          "width": 325.92,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "to-German translation task, improving over the existing best results, including",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 498.28,
          "width": 324.26,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "ensembles, by over 2 BLEU. On the WMT 2014 English-to-French translation task,",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 509.18,
          "width": 325.51,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "our model establishes a new single-model state-of-the-art BLEU score of 41.8 after",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 520.09,
          "width": 324.44,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "training for 3.5 days on eight GPUs, a small fraction of the training costs of the",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 531,
          "width": 324.26,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "best models from the literature. We show that the Transformer generalizes well to",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 541.91,
          "width": 324.27,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "other tasks by applying it successfully to English constituency parsing both with",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 552.82,
          "width": 324.27,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "large and limited training data.",
          "x": 143.87,
          "y": 563.73,
          "width": 122.4,
          "size": 9.96,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "∗",
          "x": 119.82,
          "y": 596.07,
          "width": 3.82,
          "size": 5.98,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f5",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "Equal contribution. Listing order is random. Jakob proposed replacing RNNs with self-attention and started",
          "x": 124.14,
          "y": 596.89,
          "width": 379.86,
          "size": 8.97,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "the effort to evaluate this idea. Ashish, with Illia, designed and implemented the first Transformer models and",
          "x": 108,
          "y": 606.85,
          "width": 396,
          "size": 8.97,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "has been crucially involved in every aspect of this work. Noam proposed scaled dot-product attention, multi-head",
          "x": 108,
          "y": 616.81,
          "width": 396,
          "size": 8.97,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "attention and the parameter-free position representation and became the other person involved in nearly every",
          "x": 108,
          "y": 626.78,
          "width": 396.31,
          "size": 8.97,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
        },
        {
          "text": "detail. Niki designed, implemented, tuned and evaluated countless model variants in our original codebase and",
          "x": 108,
          "y": 636.74,
          "width": 396,
          "size": 8.97,
          "angle": 0,
          "font": "g_d1_f1",
          "rtl": false
